  "description": "The Aeris AM 160 is our 160mm trail smasher! Capable of running up to 170mm forks, these frames are 160mm specific (you cannot fit a 145mm linkage to them), have more seat stay tyre clearance, revised dropouts and improved cable routing than the 145LT\n\n160mm rear travel, 160/170mm front.NEW for 2020 – rear mech cable runs under the chainstay, like the AM9NEW for 2020 – increased seatstay tyre clearanceNEW for 2020 – AM9 rear dropouts6066 tube-set, designed to give the best stiffness to weight ratioAll other parts machined, for precise tolerances and quality all roundNew self locking mini-collet axle systemOne piece hollow section yoke148 Boost rear end for maximum tyre clearance and stiffnessOne piece brake/axle assembly for maximum precision and minimum squeal230×65 Metric shock sizing1x specific rear end for maximum stiffnessISCG05 mountBottle cage mounts!\n\nOf course we’ve not dropped what made the original Aeris so popular:\n\nFantastic pedalling performance combined with a progressive shock curveExternal cable routing for improved wet weather longevityThreaded bottom bracketStealth dropper post routingMax compliment sealed cartridge bearings on all pivots27.5″ wheelsA stonkingly good price5 sizes, 3 colours and complete configuration control on all models",
